title: 'fix(sc-consensus-babe): keep the seal on headers used for equivocation reports'
doc:
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |
      BABE equivocation proofs were built from headers without their seal: block import checks for
      equivocations after verification has moved the seal into `post_digests`. The runtime verifies
      the seal of both headers, so every report failed with `InvalidEquivocationProof`.

      Block import now passes the sealed header, as the block is stored, to equivocation detection.
      No API or runtime change.
crates:
  - name: sc-consensus-babe
    bump: patch
